<article class="env-lemma" id="0EWX">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0EWX">Lemma <span data-tag="0EWX">13.27.10</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an abelian category. Assume $\mathop{\mathrm{Ext}}\nolimits ^2_\mathcal {A}(B, A) = 0$ for any pair of objects $A$, $B$ of $\mathcal{A}$. Then any object $K$ of $D^ b(\mathcal{A})$ is isomorphic to the direct sum of its cohomologies: $K \cong \bigoplus H^ i(K)[-i]$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The assumption implies that $\mathop{\mathrm{Ext}}\nolimits ^ i_\mathcal {A}(B, A) = 0$ for $i \geq 2$ and any pair of objects $A, B$ of $\mathcal{A}$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/0EWW" data-tag="0EWW">13.27.8</a>. Hence this lemma is a special case of Lemma <a href="/tag/0GM4" data-tag="0GM4">13.27.9</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>